AD SYSTEM IMPROVEMENTS — Cursor Spec
Stoqly / AITest target
=====================================

CONTEXT
-------
The ad system lives in AITest/Models/AdManager.swift and is triggered via
AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event:) calls scattered across the codebase.

The current setup has two problems:
  1. Bad triggers fire ads at inappropriate moments (sign-in, sign-out, delete
     account, password reset) — bad UX and a potential App Store review flag.
  2. The app feels completely ad-free between ad appearances because there is
     no persistent signal reminding free users that an upgrade exists.

Your job is to fix both without making the app annoying.

CRITICAL RULES (never violate):
  - modelContext.safeSave(context:) — never use try? modelContext.save()
  - Never set SubscriptionManager.isPro = true anywhere
  - Never add NavigationStack inside a sheet that already has one
  - Ad changes must respect the existing isPro guard: ads must never show
    to Pro subscribers

---

CHANGE 1 — REMOVE BAD AD TRIGGERS FROM AuthManager.swift
==========================================================

File: AITest/Models/AuthManager.swift

Remove ALL of these recordCompletion calls. They fire ads at moments that
feel punishing or manipulative, which hurts trust and can trigger App Store
rejection under guideline 4.7 (misleading ads).

DELETE these lines:
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.userSignedUp)
    (in signUp())
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.userSignedIn)
    (in signIn() AND in signInWithGoogle() — remove from both)
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.userSignedOut)
    (in signOut())
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.emailVerificationSent)
    (in sendEmailVerification())
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.passwordResetRequested)
    (in resetPassword())
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.accountDeleted)
    (in deleteAccount())
  - AdManager.shared.recordCompletion(event: AdManager.CompletionEvent.profileUpdated)
    (in updateProfile())

Keep the Analytics calls (AnalyticsManager.shared.track(...)) — only remove
the AdManager.shared.recordCompletion calls.

