CHANGE 3 — CLEAN UP AdManager.swift
=====================================

File: AITest/Models/AdManager.swift

3a. Remove orphaned event cases from CompletionEvent enum.
    DELETE these cases (they now have no callers):
      - userSignedUp
      - userSignedIn
      - userSignedOut
      - passwordResetRequested
      - accountDeleted
      - profileUpdated
      - emailVerificationSent
      - settingsChanged

3b. Update determineAdType(for:) to remove the cases you just deleted.
    The new mapping should be:

      case .inventoryCountCompleted, .exportCompleted, .barcodeScanned,
           .itemAdded, .storageCreated, .bulkImportCompleted:
          return .interstitial
      case .storageUpdated, .itemUpdated:
          return .banner

    (bulkImportCompleted is added in Change 4 below — add it here now.)

3c. Reduce actionsBeforeAd from 3 to 2.
    Change:
      private let actionsBeforeAd = 3
    To:
      private let actionsBeforeAd = 2

    Rationale: with only workflow triggers remaining, users doing real inventory
    work should see an ad roughly every 2 meaningful actions rather than 3.
    The 5-minute cooldown (minTimeBetweenAds = 300) stays unchanged — it
    prevents back-to-back ads in fast workflows.

3d. Remove the reward ad infrastructure entirely. It is not implemented, falls
    back to interstitial, and "watch an ad to unlock Pro for 24h" doesn't fit
    a business inventory tool.

    DELETE:
      - private var rewardAd: GADRewardedAd? (and the simulator stub)
      - private let rewardAdUnitID and testRewardUnitID properties
      - func loadRewardAd()
      - func showRewardAd(completion:)
      - func showRewardForPremiumPreview(feature:completion:)
      - The .reward case in AdType enum — replace with just .interstitial and .banner
      - All .reward references in loadAndShowAd() — the reward branch already
        falls back to interstitial so just remove it
      - The RewardAdTrigger struct at the bottom of the file

    After deletion, AdType enum should be:
      enum AdType { case interstitial; case banner }

