CHANGE 5 — POST-INTERSTITIAL UPSELL CHIP
==========================================

File: AITest/Models/AdManager.swift — RealAdIntegrationView struct

This is the highest-conversion placement: the user just dismissed an ad and
is mildly frustrated. Show a small native upsell chip for 3 seconds right
after the interstitial dismisses.

In RealAdIntegrationView:
  1. Add @State private var showUpgradeChip = false

  2. Add a EnvironmentObject or ObservedObject for SubscriptionManager so
     you can check isPro. If passing it via environment is complex in this
     context, read it from SubscriptionManager.shared directly.

  3. In the .fullScreenCover(isPresented: $showInterstitialOverlay) closure,
     after the InterstitialAdTrigger dismisses (inside its onDismiss callback),
     check if !SubscriptionManager.shared.isPro and if so set
     showUpgradeChip = true, then DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter(
     deadline: .now() + 3.5) { showUpgradeChip = false }

  4. Add this chip overlay inside the ZStack in RealAdIntegrationView, below
     the banner overlay:

     if showUpgradeChip && !SubscriptionManager.shared.isPro {
         VStack {
             Spacer()
             HStack(spacing: 8) {
                 Image(systemName: "sparkles")
                     .font(.system(size: 13, weight: .semibold))
                     .foregroundColor(.white)
                 Text("Remove Ads — Go Pro")
                     .font(.system(size: 13, weight: .semibold))
                     .foregroundColor(.white)
                 Spacer()
                 Text("Upgrade")
                     .font(.system(size: 12, weight: .bold))
                     .foregroundColor(Color(red: 0.051, green: 0.580, blue: 0.533))
                     .padding(.horizontal, 10)
                     .padding(.vertical, 4)
                     .background(Color.white)
                     .clipShape(Capsule())
             }
             .padding(.horizontal, 16)
             .padding(.vertical, 10)
             .background(Color(red: 0.031, green: 0.098, blue: 0.173))
             .clipShape(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 12))
             .padding(.horizontal, 12)
             .padding(.bottom, 96) // clear tab bar
             .onTapGesture {
                 showUpgradeChip = false
                 // Post a notification that InventoryAppView picks up to show
                 // the paywall — same pattern used elsewhere in the app.
                 NotificationCenter.default.post(
                     name: NSNotification.Name("stoqly.showPaywall"),
                     object: nil
                 )
             }
         }
         .transition(.move(edge: .bottom).combined(with: .opacity))
         .animation(.easeInOut(duration: 0.3), value: showUpgradeChip)
         .zIndex(10)
     }

  5. In InventoryAppView.body, add an .onReceive that listens for
     "stoqly.showPaywall" and sets showPaywall = true:

     .onReceive(NotificationCenter.default.publisher(
         for: NSNotification.Name("stoqly.showPaywall"))) { _ in
         showPaywall = true
     }

